+Aegis Advanced PoC: Carbon Optimizer, AI Operator & Explainability
+---------------------------------------------------------------
+
+This patch adds a set of PoC components intended to push Aegis forward:
+
+- services/carbon/optimizer.py : a heuristic carbon-aware optimizer service (HTTP API) that recommends placement choices.
+- services/operator/ai_operator.py : an "AI Operator" scaffold that proposes and executes safe ops actions with audit evidence.
+- services/explainability/service.py : a minimal explainability/counterfactual PoC service.
+- ops/tekton/optimizer-interceptor.yaml : example config & notes for integrating the optimizer with Tekton interceptors.
+- ops/scripts/run_carbon_optimizer.sh : helper script to call optimizer and patch a Tekton PipelineRun with an aegis.placement annotation.
+- .github/workflows/advanced_poc.yml : workflow stub for PoC validation + packaging.
+
+How these components make Aegis "ahead of its time"
+- Introduces closed-loop decision-making (optimizer) that can actively trade latency vs carbon and integrate with Tekton/interceptor hooks.
+- Provides an operator assistant that can suggest and automate routine but auditable operational changes.
+- Adds explainability surfaces (attributions & counterfactuals) to support debugging & SME review.
+- All actions are evidence-forward: operator and optimizer include evidence upload hooks for auditability.
+
+Next steps (recommended)
+1. Build and containerize the new services, push images to your registry, and deploy to the monitoring namespace.
+2. Wire Prometheus (PROM_HOST) and intensity service endpoints (INTENSITY_URL) via env vars or K8s secrets.
+3. Deploy the Tekton interceptor / webhook that calls the optimizer or configure Tekton Trigger to call ops/scripts/run_carbon_optimizer.sh as a step.
+4. Integrate AI Operator proposals into your runbooks and require human approval for unsafe actions during early rollout.
+5. Replace heuristic estimators with ML/optimization components and perform A/B tests to demonstrate carbon/latency tradeoffs.
+
+Notes & limitations
+- These components are PoCs and intentionally small. They need to be hardened (authn/authz, retries, rate-limiting),
+  replaced with production-grade telemetry mappings (candidate -> node mapping), and extended with unit+integration tests before production use.
+
